  "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to extract facts from this short Chinese novel chapter excerpt. Let me analyze the text carefully.\n\nThe text describes:\n1. A walkie-talkie (对讲机) transmitted the message \"货已经卸完\" (The goods have been unloaded)\n2. 沈北川 (Shen Beichuan) was originally standing straight\n3. His shoulders suddenly slumped\n4. The registration board in his hand almost fell into the mud\n5. He sat down on the ground along the edge of the compartment door\n6. His Adam's apple rolled twice\n7. He then loosened his clenched teeth\n8. His breathing also became longer\n9. Muddy water seeped into his trouser legs\n10. He did not stand up immediately\n\nLet me extract facts from this. I need to follow the rules:\n- Each fact is one core assertion\n- Use the 8 status values\n- Include evidence as continuous verbatim quotes (max 2 sentences)\n- Include speaker only when needed (for reported speech, cognition, etc.)\n\nLet me identify the facts:\n\n1. 对讲机传来\"货已经卸完\"的消息 - speech event, source is 对讲机 (not a person, so speaker might not apply directly, but this is a transmission)\n2. 沈北川原本站得笔直 - state (past/initial state in the scene)\n3. 沈北川听到消息后肩膀塌下去 - state change\n4. 沈北川手里的登记板差点掉进泥里 - near-miss event\n5. 沈北川顺着厢车门沿坐到地上 - action\n6. 沈北川喉结滚动两下 - action\n7. 沈北川把咬紧的牙松开 - action\n8. 沈北川呼吸变长 - state change\n9. 泥水渗进沈北川裤脚 - state\n10. 沈北川没有立刻站起来 - negative (did not stand up immediately)\n\nFor the walkie-talkie message: \"对讲机里忽然传来一句'货已经卸完'\" - this is a transmission from a walkie-talkie. The speaker here is the walkie-talkie itself, not a named person. Per the rules, I shouldn't use vague terms like \"众人\". A walkie-talkie is not a person. I think this can be recorded as a fact without a speaker, since the source is clearly a walkie-talkie and the evidence makes this clear. Or I could note \"对讲机\" as the source. Let me re-read the rules: \"speaker 用来保存'谁说的、谁认为的、信息来自谁'\" - the information comes from the walkie-talkie. I'll use \"对讲机\" as the speaker to preserve the source.\n\nActually wait - the rules say \"单条 speaker 只写一个主体\" and \"直接来源写单个人名\". A walkie-talkie is not a person. But the rule also says \"转述统一写'人名（转述自来源）'\". Hmm. The walkie-talkie is the transmission medium, not the speaker. The actual speaker is unknown - someone on the other end of the walkie-talkie. \n\nI think the safest approach is to record this as a fact that a message was received from a walkie-talkie, and since the actual person who spoke is unknown, I should note \"来源不明\" for the source. But the evidence itself says \"对讲机里忽然传来\" - so the immediate source is a walkie-talkie. \n\nLet me think about this differently. The fact is: a message \"货已经卸完\" was transmitted via walkie-talkie. This is a 已发生 event. The evidence makes the medium clear. I think I can record it with the evidence showing the walkie-talkie, and either skip the speaker (since it's not a named person speaking) or write \"来源不明\" since we don't know who actually spoke on the walkie-talkie.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"直接来源写单个人名\" - this implies if I do use a speaker, it should be a person's name. Since we don't know the person, \"来源不明\" seems appropriate per \"全文也无法确认来源时写'来源不明'\". But we do know it came through a walkie-talkie... I'll go with \"来源不明\" since the person who spoke is not identified in the text.\n\nLet me organize the facts:\n\n1. Fact: 对讲机里传来\"货已经卸完\"这一消息\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"\n   Speaker: 来源不明 (the actual person speaking through the walkie-talkie is not identified)\n\n2. Fact: 沈北川原本站得笔直\n   Status: 已发生 (this is the initial state)\n   Evidence: 沈北川原本站得笔直\n   (No speaker needed - this is narration)\n\n3. Fact: 沈北川听到消息后肩膀塌下去\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"。沈北川原本站得笔直，肩膀一下子塌下去\n   Hmm, but the evidence should be the shortest sufficient quote. Let me use: \"沈北川原本站得笔直，肩膀一下子塌下去\"\n   Actually the fact is that his shoulders slumped. The evidence \"肩膀一下子塌下去\" might be enough but to show it was a reaction, I need more context. Let me use the relevant portion.\n\nLet me reconsider. \"沈北川原本站得笔直\" and \"肩膀一下子塌下去\" are in the same sentence. The fact about the shoulder slumping is: \"沈北川肩膀塌下去\". Evidence: \"沈北川原本站得笔直，肩膀一下子塌下去\" - this gives context.\n\n4. Fact: 沈北川手里的登记板差点掉进泥里\n   Status: 已发生 (差点 = nearly happened, but it's a narrative fact that it nearly fell)\n   Evidence: 手里的登记板差点掉进泥里\n\n5. Fact: 沈北川顺着厢车门沿坐到地上\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 他顺着厢车门沿坐到地上\n\n6. Fact: 沈北川喉结滚动两下\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 喉结滚动两下\n\n7. Fact: 沈北川松开一直咬紧的牙\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 这才把一直咬紧的牙松开\n\n8. Fact: 沈北川呼吸变长\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 呼吸也跟着变长\n\n9. Fact: 泥水渗进沈北川裤脚\n   Status: 已发生\n   Evidence: 泥水渗进裤脚\n\n10. Fact: 沈北川没有立刻站起来\n    Status: 否定\n    Evidence: 泥水渗进裤脚，他没有立刻站起来\n\nWait, let me reconsider the status. \"他没有立刻站起来\" - is this 否定? The rules say \"否定：正文明确说明某事没有、并非、未曾或不会发生。\" Yes, \"没有立刻\" fits this. But \"没有立刻\" means \"did not immediately\" - he might still stand up later, but at this moment, he did not stand up. I think 否定 is appropriate, or maybe 已发生 (the fact that he didn't immediately stand up is itself an event that occurred in the narrative).\n\nActually, I think 否定 is more precise since the text explicitly says \"没有\". Let me use 否定.\n\nLet me also reconsider \"差点掉进泥里\" - is this 推测 or 已发生? \"差点\" means \"almost\" - so the registration board did NOT actually fall into the mud. But the fact is that it almost did. This is describing a near-miss that the narrative records as having occurred (the near-miss itself). I'll use 已发生 since the narrative event of \"almost falling\" is something the text records as having happened in the story.\n\nNow let me check the evidence requirements: \"evidence 必须是当前章节中的连续逐字子串，使用能独立承托该事实的最短充分原文，最多 2 句。句数按句号、问号和感叹号计算。\"\n\nLet me re-examine and construct the final output.\n\nAlso, I need to re-read the text in order:\n\"对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"。沈北川原本站得笔直，肩膀一下子塌下去，手里的登记板差点掉进泥里。他顺着厢车门沿坐到地上，喉结滚动两下，这才把一直咬紧的牙松开，呼吸也跟着变长。泥水渗进裤脚，他没有立刻站起来。\"\n\nSentences (by period):\n1. 对讲机里忽然传来一句\"货已经卸完\"。\n